# Ruling DD (Jimmy, 15 November): a placeholder wants `^Display`, and a list has none, as
# Rust's `{}` refuses a `Vec`: the program writes `{Debug xs}`, or gives the type an
# `impl ^Display`. Expected text derived by hand.
# Written by Claude on the claude-self-hosting branch; subject to change.
Listed: fn [Nat] -> Text
fn Listed xs = "all: {xs}"
